    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341-a2">

                <pb facs="0539" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg469"/>

                <head>Mr. Plumb to M.
                        Farine</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City of Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 31, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have had the honor to receive the note,
                    under date of the 29th instant, with which you have been pleased to enclose to
                    me a copy of a paper prepared by Mr. Otterbourg, late minister to Mexico,
                    regarding which you desire action at my hands as the present representative of
                    the United States in this country.</p>
                <p>In reply I am obliged to state that having to await new instructions upon the
                    general subject involved, I am unable to act in the matter at present, but will
                    hasten to transmit your note with its enclosure to the Secretary of State at
                    Washington, in order that I may receive his especial instructions in the
                    premises.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. L. PLUMB, <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires ad interim of
                            the United States.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. A. Farine,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Chief du Bureau de la Chancellerie de la Legation de
                            France, Mexico.</hi>
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
